      "short_summary": "Fast-path tryAppend() runs outside the per-partition deque lock",
      "summary": "In RecordAccumulator.append() (lines 322-333), the `synchronized (dq)` block only wraps the partitionChanged() check (lines 325-329) and closes before the fast-path `tryAppend(...)` call on line 331, so the actual batch mutation happens with no lock held.",
      "failure_scenario": "Two application threads send to the same TopicPartition concurrently with no partition switch. Both pass the partitionChanged() check, both release the dq lock, and both then call tryAppend() (line 331) concurrently on the same last ProducerBatch (deque.peekLast() returns the same object to both). ProducerBatch.tryAppend (ProducerBatch.java:168-187) is explicitly documented as \"not thread safe and external synchronization must be used when modifying it\" (ProducerBatch.java:58) and is a compound check-then-act sequence with no internal locking: it reads recordsBuilder.hasRoomFor(...), then calls recordsBuilder.append(...) (writes into the shared MemoryRecordsBuilder/ByteBuffer at the builder's current position), calls thunks.add(new Thunk(...)) on a plain ArrayList, and does the non-atomic this.recordCount++. Two unsynchronized callers can both see hasRoomFor()==true and both write, interleaving/corrupting the serialized record bytes, corrupting the ArrayList (lost or overwritten Thunk/callback entries), and racing on recordCount++ so both FutureRecordMetadata objects get the same or an inconsistent relative offset, or the batch's tracked recordCount ends up less than the number of records physically written. Separately, because peekLast() was read without holding the lock that Sender.drainBatchesForOneNode (RecordAccumulator.java:1001-1022) uses when it pollFirst()s that same batch out of the deque and then calls batch.close() outside the lock (line 1054), an appender's now-unlocked tryAppend() at line 331 can race with the Sender closing/serializing that exact batch for sending, i.e. an append can land in a batch that is concurrently being finalized or transmitted to the broker."
     }
